Route Haiku arm64 to OpenMP's pointer-va_list branch.

REAL FIX, not a cut. One OS token added to an existing conditional; no code
disabled, no dependency changed. This is the second arm64 blocker in llvm21,
reached only after the compiler-rt fix (llvm21-21.1.8-arm64-compiler-rt.patch)
cleared the first.

## The failure

After compiler-rt built, the incremental build advanced into the OpenMP runtime
and died in `openmp/runtime/src/kmp_runtime.cpp`:

    kmp_runtime.cpp:1458: error: invalid operands of types 'kmp_va_list'
                          {aka 'va_list'} and 'int' to binary 'operator!='
    kmp_runtime.cpp:1466: error: ... and 'long int' to binary 'operator=='
    kmp_runtime.cpp:1744: error: could not convert 'ap' from 'kmp_va_list'
                          {aka 'va_list'} to 'bool'

`kmp_runtime.cpp` handles `kmp_va_list` values as pointers (`!ap`, `ap == NULL`,
`ap && ...`). That is only legal when `kmp_os.h` typedefs `kmp_va_list` to
`va_list *`, not to plain `va_list`.

## Why (and why only arm64)

`KMP_OS_HAIKU` already exists in LLVM 21 (`kmp_platform.h`, keyed off
`__HAIKU__`, already in `KMP_OS_UNIX`), and the OpenMP runtime already carries a
partial Haiku port (`z_Linux_util.cpp`, `kmp_wrapper_getpid.h`, the affinity
lists). That port was done and tested on Haiku x86/x86_64, where `va_list` is
already a pointer type, so the plain-`va_list` branch happened to work.

The pointer form is selected in `kmp_os.h` only for the architectures whose
`va_list` is an aggregate AND a listed OS:

    #if (KMP_ARCH_ARM || KMP_ARCH_X86_64 || KMP_ARCH_AARCH64 || KMP_ARCH_WASM) && \
        (KMP_OS_FREEBSD || KMP_OS_NETBSD || KMP_OS_OPENBSD || KMP_OS_DRAGONFLY || \
         KMP_OS_LINUX || KMP_OS_WASI)
    typedef va_list *kmp_va_list;      // ap is va_list*  -> !ap / ap==NULL legal
    ...
    #else
    typedef va_list kmp_va_list;       // ap is va_list   -> aggregate on AArch64
    ...

Haiku was absent from the OS list, so on Haiku arm64 (`KMP_ARCH_AARCH64` set,
`va_list` an aggregate) it fell to the `#else` and the pointer expressions did
not compile. Add `KMP_OS_HAIKU` to that OS list — a BSD-branch join, exactly
what the BSDs and Linux use. The architecture guard is unchanged, so Haiku
x86/x86_64 keep the plain-`va_list` branch they already used: no behaviour
change on any existing arch.

## Proven

Deployed to the native arm64 Haiku EC2 builder (i-028584d61d2d9bf05) as a commit
appended to `llvm21-21.1.8.patchset`, regenerated with `haikuporter -e llvm21`.
On the incremental rebuild: `kmp_runtime.cpp.o` compiled, the three va_list
errors were gone (0 occurrences in the log), `libomp.so` linked and installed,
the full ninja graph completed (681/681, 0 FAILED), and `libunwind` also built
on arm64 (`libunwind.so.1.0`/`.so.1`/`.so` + headers installed) — the runtime
that had been unproven on this arch. The build then proceeded to package the
llvm21 hpkgs. No `KMP_OS_FREEBSD` site beyond this one needed a Haiku join for
the build to compile and link.

Applies to: haikuports/sys-devel/llvm/llvm21-21.1.8.recipe via its
`llvm21-21.1.8.patchset` (llvm21 has no input source package; the operative copy
is the ports-tree one under `sys-devel/llvm/`).

--- a/openmp/runtime/src/kmp_os.h
+++ b/openmp/runtime/src/kmp_os.h
@@ -219,7 +219,7 @@
 // stdarg handling
 #if (KMP_ARCH_ARM || KMP_ARCH_X86_64 || KMP_ARCH_AARCH64 || KMP_ARCH_WASM) &&  \
     (KMP_OS_FREEBSD || KMP_OS_NETBSD || KMP_OS_OPENBSD || KMP_OS_DRAGONFLY ||  \
-     KMP_OS_LINUX || KMP_OS_WASI)
+     KMP_OS_LINUX || KMP_OS_WASI || KMP_OS_HAIKU)
 typedef va_list *kmp_va_list;
 #define kmp_va_deref(ap) (*(ap))
 #define kmp_va_addr_of(ap) (&(ap))
